# 🤖 Claude Code Setup Guide

A quick reference for installing and using Claude Code from the terminal.

---

## 📋 Requirements

* Node.js
* npm
* Anthropic account

Check Node.js:

```bash
node --version
```

Check npm:

```bash
npm --version
```

---

## 📦 Installation

Install Claude Code globally:

```bash
npm install -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code
```

Check installation:

```bash
claude --version
```

---

## 🚀 Start Claude Code

Open your project directory:

```bash
cd your-project
```

Then run:

```bash
claude
```

Follow the authentication instructions shown by Claude Code.

---

## 🔑 Authentication

Claude Code may provide interactive authentication options.

If using an API key, configure the required environment variable according to the current Claude Code documentation.

Never commit API keys to GitHub.

---

## 💻 Using Claude Code in a Project

Navigate to the project:

```bash
cd your-project
```

Start Claude Code:

```bash
claude
```

You can then use Claude as an AI coding assistant while working inside the project.

---

## 🔄 Updating Claude Code

```bash
npm update -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code
```

---

## 🗑️ Uninstall

```bash
npm uninstall -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code
```

---

## 📌 Notes

Claude Code and its authentication requirements may change over time.

Check the official Anthropic documentation for the latest installation, authentication, and usage instructions.

Never share or commit your API keys, access tokens, or other credentials.
